lse,"need":false},"state_residency":{"non_need":true,"need":false}},"h15":{"text":"The Falcon Free Program is an annual program that starts each Fall term. The Falcon Free Program will cover tuition and mandatory fees for first-time undergraduate, degree-seeking Texas residents with a family-adjusted gross income (AGI) that does not exceed $100,000. Students qualify annually for up to eight semesters of full-time undergraduate enrollment. Funds are distributed until they are exhausted, so there may or may not be funds available for new students starting in spring terms. There is no separate application for the Falcon Free programs","display":true},"cite":{"H.105":{"quote":"A | Federal | $13,259,294 | $5,131,520","page":18,"line":917},"H.106":{"quote":"$3,984,647 | $54,058","page":18,"line":919},"H.107":{"quote":"waivers (which are reported below). | $2,272,437 | $5,312,856","page":18,"line":922},"H.108":{"quote":"Merit) not awarded by the college | $16,378 | $2,984,668","page":18,"line":924},"H.109":{"quote":"E | Total Scholarships/Grants | $19,532,756 | $13,483,101","page":18,"line":925},"H.110":{"quote":"G | Student loans from all sources (excluding parent loans) | $19,689,923 | $29,752,568","page":18,"line":927},"H.111":{"quote":"H | Federal Work-Study | $419,381 | $0","page":18,"line":928},"H.112":{"quote":"Excludes Federal Work-Study captured above.) | $25,690 | $0","page":18,"line":930},"H.113":{"quote":"Total Self-Help | $20,134,994 | $29,752,568","page":18,"line":931},"H.117":{"quote":"A | Federal | $13,259,294 | $5,131,520","page":18,"line":917},"H.118":{"quote":"$3,984,647 | $54,058","page":18,"line":919},"H.119":{"quote":"waivers (which are reported below). | $2,272,437 | $5,312,856","page":18,"line":922},"H.120":{"quote":"Merit) not awarded by the college | $16,378 | $2,984,668","page":18,"line":924},"H.121":{"quote":"E | Total Scholarships/Grants | $19,532,756 | $13,483,101","page":18,"line":925},"H.122":{"quote":"G | Student loans from all sources (exc